 "equations": [
  {
   "name": "Cathode voltage set by a divider",
   "expr": "VKA = Vref × (1 + R1 / R2) + R1 × Iref",
   "where": {
    "VKA": "cathode-to-anode voltage",
    "Vref": "reference input voltage, 2.5 V typ",
    "R1": "resistor from cathode to reference",
    "R2": "resistor from reference to anode",
    "Iref": "reference input current, 1.5 µA typ"
   },
   "note": "",
   "page": 4
  }
 ],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Regulation",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The device can replace a zener diode in many uses. With the reference pin tied to the cathode, the cathode sits at Vref; with a divider R1 over R2 from the cathode, the cathode sits at Vref × (1 + R1/R2) + R1 × Iref, adjustable up to 36 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Operating current",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The cathode current range is 1 mA to 100 mA; regulation needs at least 0.45 mA typ, 1.0 mA max. With the reference pin at 0 V and 36 V on the cathode, the cathode draws 0.05 µA typ, 1.0 µA max."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output capacitor",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Recommended: more than 0.1 µF from the output pin to GND to smooth the output, placed at the pin with the shortest ground return."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Stability with load capacitance",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Inside each boundary of the stability graph the part is unstable, outside it stable. With VKA = Vref the unstable region reaches about 100 mA between roughly 60 nF and 7 µF and runs down to about 1 nF and 15 µF at low current; with VKA = 5 V it stays below about 20 mA between about 25 nF and 1.5 µF. JSCJ recommends a load capacitance below one tenth of the boundary's left edge or above ten times its right edge."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature behaviour",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The equivalent temperature coefficient over the full temperature range is 50 ppm/°C typ; Vref moves 4.5 mV typ, 17 mV max between -25 °C and +85 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Land patterns",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "SOT-23: three 0.6 mm × 0.8 mm pads, the two on one side at 1.9 mm centres, the single pad 2.02 mm away in the other row. SOT-89-3L: a tab pad 1.8 mm wide and 2.8 mm long narrowing into the centre lead pad, with outer pads 0.80 mm × 1.40 mm at 1.50 mm pitch whose tops sit 0.5 mm below the tab pad's shoulder. TO-92: pads 0.80 mm × 0.70 mm at 1.27 mm pitch. All three are for reference only, in millimetres, with a general tolerance of ±0.05 mm."
  }
 ],
